From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ship the licences of the FetchContent'd C++ dependencies in
 the wheel's dist-info

cmake/*.cmake FetchContent-downloads and compiles Microsoft SEAL v4.3.3
(MIT), protobuf v3.15.8 (BSD-3-Clause), pybind11 v2.12.0
(BSD-3-Clause), xtensor 0.23.5, xtl 0.7.2 and xsimd 7.4.10 (all
BSD-3-Clause) and nlohmann/json v3.9.1 (MIT) into _tenseal_cpp,
_sealapi_cpp and libtenseal.so. SEAL's own SEAL_BUILD_DEPS in turn
fetches Microsoft GSL 4.2.1 (MIT), zlib 1.3.2 (Zlib) and zstd 1.5.7
(BSD-3-Clause) and merges zlib and zstd into its static archive.

pyproject.toml lists `license-files = ["LICENSE"]`, so the wheel carries
only TenSEAL's own Apache-2.0 text. Reproduced against the real
tenseal-0.3.18-cp312-cp312-manylinux_2_26_aarch64.manylinux_2_28_aarch64.whl
from PyPI: dist-info/licenses/ holds LICENSE alone.

Add each dependency's licence text unchanged from the pinned tag or
commit at the project root as LICENSE.<dep>, and widen license-files to
pick them up.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; this port may only touch riseproject-dev/python-wheels]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 LICENSE.gsl           | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 LICENSE.nlohmann-json | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 LICENSE.protobuf      | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 LICENSE.pybind11      | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 LICENSE.seal          | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 LICENSE.xsimd         | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 LICENSE.xtensor       | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 LICENSE.xtl           | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 LICENSE.zlib          | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 LICENSE.zstd          | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 pyproject.toml        |  2 +-
 11 files changed, 263 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

